WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.500
Meet Jacques, your cooking companion. This walkthrough uses young jackfruit tacos: an unfamiliar ingredient, a clear texture goal, and dinner for four. The recipe plan is prepared for this recording.

2
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:24.667
Start with the recipe text. For this recording, a prepared plan loads into the actual app. This is a scripted demonstration, not a live recipe-generation benchmark.

3
00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:34.933
First, drain and rinse twenty ounces of young green jackfruit. Jacques keeps one active step on screen, with a short instruction and an illustrated reference.

4
00:00:34.933 --> 00:00:43.533
Cut away the tough triangular cores. The useful cue is specific: separate the firm core from the softer pieces that will pull apart.

5
00:00:43.533 --> 00:00:53.867
Now shred with your fingers or two forks. The goal is distinct strands, not a paste. That visible finish line makes an unfamiliar ingredient easier to handle.

6
00:00:53.867 --> 00:01:04.667
The question cards follow the current step: how fine should the strands be, and how do I avoid a mushy texture? This recording shows the prompts, not a live answer.

7
00:01:04.667 --> 00:01:15.300
Soften onion and garlic in oil for about five minutes. Then add the jackfruit, chili powder, cumin, smoked paprika, orange juice, and soy sauce.

8
00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:27.533
Start the twelve-minute timer. Simmer and press the jackfruit into the pan. The timer is working in the app; the cooking itself is condensed here. Look for lightly browned edges and distinct strands.

9
00:01:27.533 --> 00:01:40.033
Watch Me displays the recipe cue beside its capture panel. In this build, it checks media capture only. It does not assess the food. These illustrations are references, not camera evidence.

10
00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:54.133
Fill eight corn tortillas and finish with lime and cilantro. That is the Jacques walkthrough: a recipe broken into manageable actions, visual cues, useful questions, and a timer. Dinner, one step at a time.
